nd by the test:** the lexical field is per passage, not per movement — a5v6zxm still qualifies on "through all phases" while its extension/flexion is only "active". The term list was written before it was run on these two quotes and was not changed to separate them; the evaluator sees the terms and judges the movement. So whether sjm4bip DP recovers to 3 is an open question the A/B answers, not a result I engineered. · **Chris's reasoning has to be in the store to count.** Mark's relay is why the rule was written, but a comment by Mark is not ingested (author must be a mentor, §6.3) and relayed reasoning is not Chris's words. Ask Chris for two sentences on a5v6zxm's thread (the two points above); ingested automatically as `chris_comment` on `session:a5v6zxm`, self-excluded from that session, retrieved for the others — then a5v6zxm's exemplar bounds with its reason attached. · Next: `--reuse --label v5b` on all three, `ab --labels base,v5,v5b`. Adopt 5b if it keeps v5's gains; the sjm4bip DP line is the one to watch, and a5v6zxm's DP must stay 2.
