scorecard (assembler `chunkIndex[].scores`), never from the evaluator; lowest ceiling wins; no floor (stronger never raises — that was the inflating direction); logged in `guards_applied`; same guard in `normalizeLine` so practice matches. `exemplar_anchor` string kept (UI reads it). Template trimmed to 2,999 tok with no rule removed. Selftests: bound cases (equal clamps, weaker clamps, stronger inert, misreported N ignored, non-exemplar id invalid, unders untouched, section averages recomputed). · **Prediction, from the baseline anchors as written:** Evaluate 3→2 on all three (a5v6zxm weaker on vs_intent; sjm4bip and 7uk7lnh equal to a both_made line Chris scored 2); a5v6zxm's other five lines stay 3 — their anchors are equal to 3-lines (sjm4bip CE/DP, 7uk7lnh Rx/Bio) or genuinely stronger on a graded field (Eq: effect stated) — so expected ≈ exact 8/18, Ev 3/3, mean Δ ≈ +0.22, no under worsened (the three unders all have equal/weaker anchors and scores already ≤ N). · **Not run here:** `--reuse --label v5` on all three + `npm run ab -- --labels base,v5`. Adopt only if no line regresses. · Decided: the desired-outcome gate is **untestable on these cards** — all three sessions name the intended outcome (vs_intent partial/made on each), so it would fire on none; parked in §17 until a session that omits it. The 51:02 C&E item is **not tunable from counts**: all three have 0 complete, similar partial profiles, and Chris gave 2 / 3 / 2 — his "one run's worth" and specificity are depth judgments the inventory does not carry; recorded, no change. **a5v6zxm is the open problem**: on the inventory it is the strongest of the three (11 connections, 8 unprompted, ideal with 5 fundamentals, equipment effect stated) and Chris scored it lowest; his reasoning for it is nowhere in the store (the 9/21 call is not transcribed). Ask him, or get that call.
